  "id": "roberts-syndrome",
  "term": "Roberts syndrome",
  "definition": "Roberts syndrome is a cohesinopathy, also called SC phocomelia syndrome, caused by bi-allelic mutations in the ESCO2 gene. It is associated with a range of developmental problems that can include growth retardation, intellectual disability, microcephaly, and congenital abnormalities.",
